-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:18c1f12a44836f92efba68c66fc96d9f3fb39f7fa64efd0d98fb2fb69b8e0778","file":"preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":60,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"dc09f9a663ba78905625513b8470a7c142e5825d32f4f473ada7080781798bd0","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:18c1f12a44836f92efba68c66fc96d9f3fb39f7fa64efd0d98fb2fb69b8e0778","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L60"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{m:main}\nThe following statements hold.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item A finite nonempty lattice is representable if and only if it satisfies\nthe finite colored-graph criterion in \\Cref{f:criterion}.\nFor each candidate graph size the criterion is decidable by a finite test.\n\\item There is no deterministic Turing machine that, given the order table\nof a finite nonempty lattice, always halts and decides \\(\\mathcal R(L)\\).\n\\item There is a nonrepresentable finite lattice \\(L_0\\) of minimum\ncardinality, specified by the finite formulas in \\Cref{sec:minimum}.\nEvery finite lattice of smaller cardinality is representable, and\n\\(\\lvert L_0\\rvert>7\\).\n\\item Given the order table of a finite nonempty lattice \\(L\\), it is\nundecidable whether \\(L\\cong[H,G]\\) for some finite group \\(G\\) and\nsubgroup \\(H\\le G\\), where \\([H,G]\\) is the full subgroup interval.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
